      "id": "p0194-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Sans runs a hot dog stand in Hotland. If the player buys enough hot dogs, Sans invents new replacements for the word \"hot dog\". Because these silly name variations play with English punctuation and spelling, the translator tweaked them to work smoothly in Japanese:",
        "raw": "Sans runs a hot dog stand in Hotland. If the player buys enough hot dogs, Sans\ninvents new replacements for the word \"hot dog\". Because these silly name\nvariations play with English punctuation and spelling, the translator tweaked\nthem to work smoothly in Japanese:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
