    {
      "id": "p0194-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "During the game’s localization process, Toby often wrote notes to himself to later share with the localization team. In one such note, Toby came up with an idea for a comical \"hot dog\" abbreviation in Japanese: ットdog (tto dog). Essentially, the \"ho\" part of \"hot dog\" would be dropped, and the word \"dog\" would be left in English.",
        "raw": "During the game's localization process, Toby often wrote notes to himself to\nlater share with the localization team. In one such note, Toby came up with\nrd\nan idea for a comical \"hot dog\" abbreviation in Japanese: \"/\n0 g (tto dog).\nEssentially, the \"ho\" part of\"hot dog\" would be dropped, and the word \"dog\"\nwould be left in English.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29395819,
          0.54672143,
          0.8878303,
          0.63195714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29141301,
          0.54600714,
          0.89728819,
          0.63302857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          29,
          30,
          31,
          32,
          33,
          34,
          35
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "本地化期间，Toby 经常给自己写笔记，准备之后分享给团队。其中一条设想了日语里一个滑稽的“热狗”缩写：「ットdog」（tto dog）。也就是删掉 hot dog 开头的“ho”，而 dog 仍保留英语。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
