      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The idea behind Toby's new \"hot dog\" word was quite clever - the consonant extending character \"/ almost never appears at the beginning of a Japanese word, and the decision to keep \"dog\" in English makes the Japanese abbreviation even sillier. Although he never pitched this suggestion to the localization team, it's another clear sign that Toby was actively involved in the localization process of his own game.",
